  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Chandrakant Jotiram Khirsagar vs State Of Maharashtra on 17 April, 2023 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai 2023:Bhc-As:11865 Megha 22_aba_927_2022.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.927 Of 2022 Chandrakant Jotiram Khirsagar ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent ... Mr. Hrishikesh S. Shinde i/b. Mr. Shailesh Chavan for the Applicant. Mr. R.M. Pethe, App for Respondent-State. Coram: Smt. Anuja Prabhudessai, J. Dated : 17th April, 2023. P. C. :- 1.",
    "facts": "3. The aforesaid crime was registered pursuant to the Megha 22_aba_927_2022.doc complaint lodged by Prashant Kuchekar, Food Safety Officer alleging that Kamti Police station has seized one truck with sachets of Vimal tobacco, V1 Tobacco and R.M.d. Pan Masala etc. total worth Rs.29,28,000/-. The driver was taken in custody. It is stated that the said seized material is banned in the State of Maharashtra, despite which the Applicant herein has transported the same in the State of Maharashtra. It is stated that issue regarding applicability of Section 328 of the IPC in such cases is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. The other offences are not of serious nature. The Applicant was granted interim protection on 07/04/2022 and the said protection is continued from time to time. The records reveal that the Applicant was directed to report on 14th and 15th April, 2022 and further as and when required by the investigating agency. Almost a year has passed since the said dates.",
    "arguments": "(ii) The Applicant shall report to the concerned investigating officer as and when required by the investigating Officer; (iii)The Applicant shall not tamper with the prosecution evidence and or influence the witnesses in any manner.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "(ii) The Applicant shall report to the concerned investigating officer as and when required by the investigating Officer; (iii)The Applicant shall not tamper with the prosecution evidence and or influence the witnesses in any manner."
  },
